        "one_line": "Chios and Lesbos exported the most sought-after wines of the Greek Aegean, shipped west in amphorae stamped with each island's own seal. Chios marked its jars with a sphinx to stop mainland forgeries, and its wine was poured at four separate Roman triumphs, the first foreign vintage ever served at one. Lesbian wine had rivaled Chian since Homer's day and stayed prized through the 2nd century.",
